t condition and recommendations\r\nProvision of outputs in line with industry standards and client requirements\r\n\r\nHow to Apply:\r\nSuppliers must express interest through CompeteFor to receive further tender information, including lot structure and next steps.\r\n\r\n\r\nAbout the buyer's selection process:\r\nRegional Approach:\r\nThe framework will be structured into regional lots across England, allowing suppliers to bid for one or multiple regions based on:\r\n\r\nAvailability of specialist drainage equipment and vehicles\r\nOperational capacity and response capability\r\nLocal presence and mobilisation times\r\nAbility to deliver both planned and reactive services\r\nSuitable Suppliers\r\nThis opportunity is aimed at suppliers who demonstrate:\r\n\r\nProven experience in drainage maintenance and CCTV survey services\r\nCapability to deliver inspection, cleaning and emergency drainage works\r\nAccess to trained operatives and specialist equipment\r\nStrong health, safety, environmental and quality performance\r\nExperience working in live, constrained or high-risk environments (e.g. highways, rail, infrastructure)\r\nAbility to produce accurate survey reports and data outputs\r\nSMEs and regional drainage contractors are encouraged to apply	\N	c298cefe-d98e-43a7-b9a2-0c900da44efb	\N	b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002	United Kingdom	\N	1000000	GBP	Public Tender	Open	\N	https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/cab54caa-0fe7-49f3-9a4b-385a477166bd	\N	\N	\N	{"Civil engineering support services",UK,"Contracts Finder"}	2026-07-21	2026-07-21	e9118ceb435abddbe49bb908541252a1643f533c3a68a497dd2afac9d0ef7330	'24/7':208B 'abil':315B,379B 'access':351B 'accur':382B 'across':32B,70B,285B 'aim':328B 'align':45B 'allow':287B 'appli':251B,396B 'approach':276B 'assess':96B 'asset':155B,234B 'avail':298B 'base':296B 'bid':290B 'blockag':131B,203B 'build':134B 'buyer':271B 'bypass':180B 'call':42B,209B 'capabl':211B,309B,342B 'capac':306B 'catch':145B 'cctv':91B,22