77224131-0c05-4997-9ea9-4df1933bfd87	ocds-b5fd17-897ccb76-e9d2-48f9-b386-111335f7bc54	RA359362 - Occupational Health	Please see specification below. Please contact lewis.atkinson@londonenergyltd.com with any proposals or clarifications. \r\n\r\ni.\tLondonEnergy Ltd ("LEL") is seeking to appoint a suitable qualified and experienced Occupational Health ("OH") provider to deliver a comprehensive, responsive and proactive Occupational Health Service to support the health, wellbeing and attendance management of our 350+ workforce.\r\n\r\nThe appointed provider will work in partnership with LEL to deliver high-quality occupational health services that support employee wellbeing, promote fitness for work, facilitate effective case management and assist the organisation in meeting its legal and statutory obligations under relevant health and safety and employment legislation.\r\n\r\nLEL employs a diverse workforce operating across office-based, operational and engineering environments, with employees undertaking a range of safety-critical and physically demanding roles. As such, the Occupational Health Service must be capable of providing timely, pragmatic and evidence-based advice to managers, employees and the Human Resources team.\r\n\r\nThe successful provider will be expected to deliver a modern, flexible and customer-focused service incorporating both remote and face-to-face appointments where appropriate, supported by secure digital systems, robust management information and effective account management.\r\n\r\nii.\tGeneral\r\n•\tAbility to book face-to-face OH appointments where the case would benefit from a face-to-face appt.\r\n•\tLocal clinic or local hub where face-to-face appointments can be held located close to Eco Park, Tottenham Hale or Liverpool Street. \r\n•\tAbility to book urgent OH appointments and not just rely on cancellations being available to do so.\r\n•\tRegular meetings with our client relationship manager.\r\n•\tAbility to have a case conference call with the OH doctor, if possible, for complex cases.      \r\n•\tSupply of useful data to us by OH provider on a quarterly basis to feed into the Board Report.\r\n•\tUser friendly OH portal to make referrals on and then be able to see the reports on and historical reports for employees too.    \r\n\r\niii.\tTechnology\r\n•\tSecure online portal\r\n•\tAbility to communicate directly with physician \r\n•\tAbility to integrate with HR systems in future / API's\r\n•\tElectronic referral and reporting\r\n\r\niv.\tData and Reporting\r\n\r\nOur existing providers ability to pull any data/reporting is non-existent. Would like to see a secure portal and understand what management information can be provided on a month basis i.e.\r\n•\tReferral volumes\r\n•\tReferral reasons\r\n•\tDepartment trends\r\n•\tAbsence hotspots\r\n•\tSafety Critical roles\r\n•\tDrivers\r\n•\tShift work\r\n\r\n\r\nv.\tAdditional Services\r\n•\tErgonomic assessments\r\n•\tManager training\r\n•\tHealth/wellbeing initiatives\r\n - To access this competition: login to https://suppliers.multiquote.com and view the opportunity RA359362. Not registered on MultiQuote - visit https://suppliers.multiquote.com then register and quote RA359362 as the reason for registration. Any queries please contact MultiQuote on 0151 482 9230.	\N	4bc093fc-23b2-499d-b869-07543183acc7	\N	b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002	United Kingdom	\N	\N	\N	Public Tender	Open	\N	https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/376884b7-36dc-4e75-95f2-e35f4bb9755a	\N	\N	\N	{"Business services: law, marketing, consulting, recruitment, printing and security",UK,"Contracts Finder"}	2026-07-31	2026-07-20	e885fa48d62cfc085d98225aaca65f6d5810c11f98d5d96b835b000ae5a20c4d	'0151':442B '350':53B '482':443B '9230':444B 'abil':197B,242B,266B,329B,335B,356B 'abl':312B 'absenc':391B 'access':409B 'account':193B 'across':109B 'addit':400B 'advic':147B 'api':343B 'appoint':23B,56B,180B,205B,228B,247B 'appropri':182B 'appt':217B 'assess':403B 'assi