fae88396-aa0d-4e54-9f50-f28815b9e9d5	ocds-b5fd17-82d1db33-40ea-4450-bdf8-818dd672f50b	Opportunity to Tender - Craneage - Regional Framework Lots (England) - J. Murphy & Sons	J. Murphy & Sons invites expressions of interest from experienced track matting suppliers / subcontractor for inclusion on a framework of regional lots across England, supporting major infrastructure programmes.\r\nThe framework will provide opportunities to supply and install temporary access solutions on a call off basis, aligned to project locations and regional delivery teams.\r\n\r\nProject Portfolio Includes:\r\nNetwork Rail CP7\r\nTransPennine Route Upgrade (TRU)\r\nPeel Ports\r\nOther rail and infrastructure projects across England\r\n\r\nScope of Services:\r\nThe framework will cover the provision of operated crane hire services, including:\r\n\r\nSupply of mobile cranes ranging from 25 tonnes to 130 tonnes capacity, with certified operators\r\nLifting operations in support of general construction and civil engineering works\r\nExecution of standard and complex lifting activities, including confined or restricted site environments\r\nProvision of lift planning and appointed person services where required\r\nSupport for structural installations, drainage, earthworks and concrete operations\r\nDelivery of both planned lifting activities and reactive call out services"\r\n\r\n\r\nHow to Apply:\r\nSuppliers must express interest through CompeteFor to receive further tender information, including lot structure and next steps.\r\n\r\n\r\nAbout the buyer's selection process:\r\nRegional Approach:\r\nThe framework will be structured into regional lots across England, enabling suppliers to bid for one or multiple regions based on:\r\n\r\nFleet availability and crane capacity range (25t-130t)\r\nOperator availability and competency\r\nLocal depot presence and response capability\r\nAbility to support projects within the designated regions	\N	c298cefe-d98e-43a7-b9a2-0c900da44efb	\N	b0000000-0000-0