e34b78d1-ce69-43d6-b443-5ac38952f0da	ocds-b5fd17-add2d22c-81b0-444a-acba-c736dc121122	Swindon Integrated Sexual Health Services	Swindon Borough Council invites expressions of interest from suitably qualified and experienced service providers for the provision of Integrated Sexual Health Services. \r\n\r\nThe Contract Notice invites offers under the Competitive Process of the Provider Selection Regime (PSR) Regulations. \r\n\r\nSwindon Borough Council has a statutory duty to commission open-access sexual and reproductive health services. This will be a single-lot model delivering clinical services, digital access, postal testing, Long-Acting Reversible Contraception (LARC) in GPs, outreach and prevention. This model is the preferred option following a structured Preliminary Market Engagement exercise and reflects the shift toward digital-first, outcomes-based, prevention-focused sexual health systems.  \r\n\r\nThe initial contract term will be for 60 months with an option to extend for a further 48 months (2 periods of 24 months) for a potential total contract term of 9 years. The guaranteed contract value is £13.1m across the initial 5-year contract term and £23.58m across the potential total 9-year contract term.  \r\n\r\nFor transparency, this value is presented differently to the indicative value used during Preliminary Market Engagement (PME), where estimated Out of Area (OOA) income was included within the total contract value. \r\n\r\nOut of Area (OOA) income (estimated at c.£350,000 per annum) is excluded from this value, as it is non-guaranteed, activity-dependent income and not funded through the Swindon Public Health Grant. OOA income, in line with national sexual health cross-charging guidance, will be retained by the provider and mandatorily reinvested to support the delivery of the commissioned service. \r\n\r\nThe exclusion of estimated OOA income does not represent a reduction in the anticipated overall value of service income available to the provider; rather, it reflects the separation of guaranteed commissioner funding from non-guaranteed activity-based income.	\N	b358a57b-ba1a-481f-b4f7-4076dff666d8	\N	b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002	United Kingdom	\N	23580000	GBP	Public Tender	Open	\N	https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/7ab72679-9da5-470d-88c0-b61f3edf3e88	\N	\N	\N	{"IT services: consulting, software development, Internet and support",UK,"Contracts Finder"}	2026-09-01	2026-07-14	ad4fd6ffdbd0a3bb141186ff625de0126ea2884e7a4a07e9dab4d72f96daed9b	'000':215B '13.1':155B '2':136B '23.58':165B '24':139B '350':214B '48':134B '5':160B '60':124B '9':148B,171B 'access':55B,73B 'across':157B,167B 'act':78B 'activ':230B,308B 'activity-bas':307B 'activity-depend':229B 'annum':217B 'anticip':284B 'area':196B,208B 'avail':290B 'base':110B,309B 'borough':7B,45B 'c':213B 'charg':252B 'clinic':70B 'commiss':52B,269B 'commission':301B 'competit':35B 'consult':313C 'contracept':80B 'contract':29B,119B,145B,152B,162B,173B,204B,320C 'council':8B,46B 'cross':251B 'cross-charg':250B 'deliv':69B 'deliveri':266B 'depend':231B 'develop':315C 'differ':181B 'digit':72B,106B 'digital-first':105B 'duti':50B 'engag':98B,190B 'estim':193B,211B,274B 'exclud':219B 'exclus':272B 'exercis':99B 'experienc':17B 'express':10B 'extend':130B 'finder':321C 'first':107B 'focus':113B 'follow':93B 'fund':235B,302B 'gps':83B 'grant':241B 'guarante':151B,228B,300B,306B 'guidanc':253B 'health':4A,26B,59B,115B,240B,249B 'includ':200B 'incom':198B,210B,232B,243B,276B,289B,310B 'indic':184B 'initi':118B,159B 'integr':2A,24B 'interest':12B 'internet':316C 'invit':9B,31B 'larc':81B 'line':245B 'long':77B 'long-act':76B 'lot':67B 'm':156B,166B 'mandatorili':261B 'market':97B,189B 'model':68B,88B 'month':125B,135B,140B 'nation':247B 'non':227B,305B 'non-guarante':226B,304B 'notic':30B 'offer':32B 'ooa':197B,209B,242B,275B 'open':54B 'open-access':53B 'option':92B,128B 'outcom':109B 'outcomes-bas':108B 'outreach':84B 'overal':285B 'per':216B 'pe