8bf1a342-0d5f-491e-a34f-66bec1399fc6	ocds-b5fd17-adeb6f21-b1bf-4fa0-b2a3-e9eed9b4433b	Supply of Bodyworn Energy Data Logger	Unite Procurement UK Limited (part of Unite Holding SE), on behalf of the Ministry of Defence, is seeking suppliers to join the Unite Procurement Platform to support the Supply of Bodyworn Energy Data Logger. The procurement covers the supply of specialist power measurement equipment designed to accurately measure and log power consumption from soldier-carried and operated systems.\r\n\r\nObjectives\r\n•\tPurchase of equipment capable of measuring the power usage of operator-carried systems\r\n•\tContinued storage and issue of power loggers to projects, thereby informing overall power demand\r\n•\tMeasurement and data processing of power information\r\n•\tNett Warrior connector compatibility\r\nExclusions\r\n•\tProlonged data analysis\r\n•\tEquipment updates or upgrades\r\n•\tAdaptors required for non-compatible equipment (responsibility of the system under test)\r\n•\tOperating costs for the equipment (a secondary activity for personnel already engaged in the projects under test)\r\n6. Technical Requirements\r\n•\tMust measure power draw from a battery source to a connected portable system\r\n•\tMust be compatible with Nett Warrior connectors\r\n•\tMust export data at Official classification\r\n•\tMust be supplied with appropriate connectors to interface with standard computers (expected: USB)\r\nAcceptance Criteria\r\nUpon delivery, a brief trial of each item will be conducted, including monitoring of power used by a representative system, followed by upload of data to a standalone laptop. Successful completion of this trial will constitute acceptance and clearance for use in future activities.\r\nAcceptance criteria include successful power measurement recording, accurate data export, and successful data transfer to standard computer systems via USB interface.\r\n\r\nHow to Apply\r\nInterested suppliers should register their interest by contacting Unite Procurement UK Limited and provide details of their product range, technical specifications, and delivery capabilities. Further information on the onboarding process for the Unite Procurement Platform will be provided upon expression of interest.\r\nUnite Procurement UK Limited does not intend to appoint a sole supplier for this requirement. Instead, multiple suppliers may be onboarded to the Unite Procurement Platform to ensure a diverse and competitive supply base, supporting flexibility and choice for the Ministry of Defence and associated organisations.\r\nSuppliers are encouraged to express their interest by the stated closing date to ensure early consideration. However, applications to join the Unite Procurement Platform will be welcome at any time beyond the initial deadline. Unite Procurement UK Limited reserves the right to review and onboard new suppliers on a rolling basis to meet evolving requirements and to maintain a dynamic and responsive supplier network.\r\nFor any enquiries and interest, please email defence.support@unite.eu with the subject title TSS 698 Opportunity.	\N	a72f0b4c-4bdd-4e23-b0c2-07114b402f0b	\N	b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002	United Kingdom	\N	120000	GBP	Public Tender	Open	\N	https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/a7f6811e-5027-41dc-866a-d7de03d29d1a	\N	\N	\N	{"Electronic equipment",UK,"Contracts Finder"}	2026-08-05	2026-07-08	ae1dce6130cc1c36269af87361621e8242140e5d370cd63a1eeb42d083714ed8	'6':144B '698':421B 'accept':186B,224B,232B 'accur':53B,239B 'activ':134B,231B 'adaptor':114B 'alreadi':137B 'analysi':109B 'appli':255B 'applic':361B 'appoint':306B 'appropri':177B 'associ':342B 'base':331B 'basi':394B 'batteri':153B 'behalf':17B 'beyond':374B 'bodyworn':3A,37B 'brief':191B 'capabl':70B,279B 'carri':62B,79B 'choic':335B 'classif':172B 'clearanc':226B 'close':354B 'compat':105B,119B,162B 'competit':329B 'complet':218B 'comput':183B,248B 'conduct':198B 'connect':157B 'connector':104B,166B,178B 'conside