bdb3fa78-7c46-4e54-bdc4-c8a662b51b11	ocds-b5fd17-59d0b0c3-4ffe-4ba9-a9ad-b3c792c54f08	BBV Sublot 4 - HSST1020 - Cut & Bent Steel Reinforcement - Curzon Approach Viaducts	This scope is for the provision of cut and bent steel reinforcement for Curzon Approach Viaducts. The supplier should review the steel reinforcement drawings and cut and bent steel in accordance with the drawings and bar bending schedules provided by the Contractor. The bars should be cut and bent at the supplier's premises and comply with the relevant BBV/HS2 specification and relevant British Standards:\r\n      \r\n      •\tAll hot rolled and cold worked steel bars shall conform to BS EN 10080 and BS 4449 Grades B500B or B500C\r\n      •\tBS 8666 from 2005 and eventually 2020 Scheduling, dimensioning, bending and cutting of Steel Reinforcement for Concrete\r\n      •\tThe mandrel diameter for bending bars shall comply with Clause 8.3 of BS EN 1992-1-1.\r\n      •\tCARES product acceptance scheme for steel reinforcement\r\n      •\tCouplers shall be TA1A CARES certified\r\n      \r\n      The supplier should also provide any couplers including threading and any relating protection of the re-bars. Bars should be delivered to site labelled with the references of the bar bending schedule and pre-slung to facilitate safe unloading. Supplier should also provide any method statements and their related risk assessment as well as all relevant quality documentation such as quality management plan, grade mill certificates for the supplied re-bar, CARES certificates, CARS certificates and technical data sheets for the couplers, samples for testing (if required) and any other required to demonstrate compliance with the specification and industry standards. \r\n      \r\n      The package covers three key activities spanning over the next 2 and half years. These are the construction of the complex Curzon no. 3 post tensioned reinforced concrete deck and its finishes with 6220m3 of concrete and 2384tonnes of reinforcement remaining, the construction of the deck finishing works across the remaining assets of Curzon Approach (Curzon no. 2, Curzon no. 1 and Duddeston Viaduct) with ....tonnes remaining and the fabrication of the precast concrete slabs for Curzon Approach at BBV Kingsbury Yard with ....tonnes remaining.\r\n\r\nAdditional information: Suppliers should be aware of the scale of this project and should assess their internal capabilities to be able to carry out the intended scope of work, prior to completing this expression of interest (EOI).	\N	23eadffe-2474-4573-a5de-7f73963d211d	\N	b0000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002	United Kingdom	\N	2500000	GBP	Public Tender	Open	\N	https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/dd4927e0-8991-4aa8-9ea6-ecb6676e7d86	\N	\N	\N	{"Structural steel erection work for structures",UK,"Contracts Finder"}	2026-05-20	2026-05-13	4c40a48352c43ba63ea9849dda4a965ea6cf66321de209f93d49309ed3fe8aba	'-1':130B,131B '1':308B '10080':90B '1992':129B '2':258B,305B '2005':101B '2020':104B '2384tonnes':285B '3':271B '4':3A '4449':93B '6220m3':281B '8.3':125B '8666':99B 'abl':353B 'accept':134B 'accord':42B 'across':296B 'activ':253B 'addit':333B 'also':148B,188B 'approach':10A,26B,302B,325B 'assess':197B,347B 'asset':299B 'awar':338B 'b500b':95B 'b500c':97B 'bar':47B,55B,84B,120B,162B,163B,175B,218B 'bbv':1A,327B 'bbv/hs2':71B 'bend':48B,107B,119B,176B 'bent':6A,21B,39B,60B 'british':75B 'bs':88B,92B,98B,127B 'capabl':350B 'car':221B 'care':132B,143B,219B 'carri':355B 'certif':212B,220B,222B 'certifi':144B 'claus':124B 'cold':81B 'complet':364B 'complex':268B 'compli':67B,122B 'complianc':241B 'concret':114B,275B,283B,321B 'conform':86B 'construct':265B,290B 'contract':377C 'contractor':53B 'coupler':139B,151B,229B 'cover':250B 'curzon':9A,25B,269B,301B,303B,306B,324B 'cut':5A,19B,37B,58B,109B 'data':225B 'deck':276B,293B 'deliv':166B 'demonstr':240B 'diamet':117B 'dimens':106B 'document':204B 'draw':35B,45B 'duddeston':310B 'en':89B,128B 'eoi':369